Z||000000||My 88 Coupe||09-17-2001||01:49 AM||||Ok guys,<BR>Thanks for the input... I didnt get bet by a Metro, it was my sisters 91 Storm Gsi... Yes I have drove a v-6 Fiero..ughhh it was ok I didnt buy it got a 88 300zx nt but was happy with it fun car and semi quick but too much cost up keep(the old owner didnt take care of it in two years I had over 8,000 in the car that counts the 3,000 I gave for it) so now it sets in the carport un driven hate it now! The Fiero I drove was a 88 Auto v-6 didnt seem fast on the highway,the other one was a 85 v-6 4 speed,it didnt like how it trashed on the highway with high rpms! I have unplugged my Tcc as it goes in at 30 mph and drives me nuts in town and highway here is mostly 55-65 Louisiana of course so my rpms are not to bad! btw the 30-35 isnt that low for it to go into lock up? and my car goes out of first at 35 if I hold it down from a stop anyway to adjust this to maybe even 40-45 I held it in first till 40 seemed ok to me wasnt too bad! and next weight I know dump the spare tire Jack,what else? padding under the carpet? anything else like the honey comb behind the bumper dont seem like they would help that much in a wreck? but they look light also? anyway what else is there for a Duke? also I want more sound a deeper sound I had a few people say to cut the cat off and put a cherry bomb there and use my normal muffler and it would sound great! but wont this let less air out? I dont want it to sound like my 87 duke 5 speed with the glass pack muffler was a little too much over kill!!! Anyway ideals are nice and what about a 3.1? I know computer,wire,motor,fuel pump what else would I have to have and would this be nice? I had a friend with a 3.1 Beretta 3 speed auto and I love how it would run on the highway! My tech 4 is great in town just I want more than what the Duke and 2.8 gives on the highway! I am sure a-lot of us are the same way! I love the Duke and wish ther was someway to make it do good on the highway without spending 1100.00 for that you can get the 3.1 here and maybe spedn another 200-300 in extra parts! and the 1100.00 I was told makes the 2.5 maybe semi a match for the 2.8 so I have changed my thoughts on my Duke as sad as it makes me but oh well its a good motor for the 84 fiero driver that just enjoys driving the car and dont like to race with a Volvo and get whooped! yes my friend has a 84 240 turbo intercooled and can stomp my car dead on the highway and only has 160 hp but it is a Turbo and hasd 160 as to our 90-121? And I have heard that our cars have anywhere from 90-121 for 88 tech 4's? I do notice a slight more power over my 84 and 87 but not too much! so what is righ on my hp?<BR>Thanks guys<BR>||||reg||4
