Z||000002||My 88 Coupe||09-17-2001||02:34 AM||||Thanks for the comments! May your Quad 4 live many long miles before it blows up! I have heard lot about them, several friends have had Quad 4 H.O. motors and even my step mom. Sure it has more power but it has worse reliability than say a Yugo! I love the power and all but, I would have stuck with the Tech 4 and worked it up much cheaper to fix when it blows up! The Quad will also blow up so either way you are going to have power and blow up! You threw your salt so now I have thrown mine back<BR>Have a good Day<BR>Have a good one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000003||Leper||09-17-2001||04:43 AM||||Honestly, what are you asking?<BR>I read that paragraph 3 times now and far all I can figure is that you want to know what an 88 iron duke makes for HP, it's 96. If you think you can get 180hp out of it and keep it even semi reliable, you won't. Quad 4's have their problems, but they can be remedied. If you want cheap reliable hp then go with the 3.1 swap. If you don't like the v6 4 speed gearing then look for a v6 with a 5 speed or an auto. As for the tcc, it should lock up in 3rd gear when going at a steady speed. You might want to check your tv cable on your transmission as it's possible you may have a shifting problem. If you want to strip the car down to make it lighter, you can basically take everything that isn't neccesary for you to drive down the road. You can get more HP out of the iron duke but it's easier to do with the earlier year motors becasue you can adjust the timing to suit the changes and most of the performance parts were made for the earlier motors. You can adapt them to fit the 88, but you would be better off just converting to a v6. You can basically use all of the v6 fiero parts on the 3.1 block to do the swap. So search for people that have done the 4 to 6 swap. I have heard that replacing the cat with a cherry bomb makes the car sound good, but I don't know anyone that has done it to a 4 cyl. It should let the exhaust flow freer than with the stock cat. It's also illegal to do since you're removing an emissions device. It's not my fault that you raced a car with almost twice the hp and lost (the volvo, not the geo). I havent heard Standard complain of any reliability issues with his quad 4 but I know the reputation of the motor and still think it's a viable swap for anyone that wants to try it. This is the last time I will reply to one of your topics as I believe you are a troll and for someone who has only posted 4 times, you sure are cocky.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Galen||09-17-2001||04:53 AM||||88's have a special button that you push and it'll give it super speed. hehe.. I'm with Leper, I dont get what you're asking. 88 dukes had 98hp.. as for the quad, if I had the time and the nerve(and money) I'd do one without hesitation. As Standard has told me he loves that car. This is called a Fiero Community, When you live and/or work in a community, it is not a very good thing to do to come up and smack other ppl that live/work there and talk sh!t about their cars. troll!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/g-flag-sig.gif">  <FONT COLOR="purple">1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe</FONT> - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>Fierolinks</A>||||reg||1
